% The page is priced in whole units. The module is the line, 14 pt square: the
% paragraph indent is one module, the text block is 23 by 40 of them.
% Black ink and one accent, the colour of the flag. The opening engravings
% use black and white; the accent belongs to the proof notation.
% A proof cell is a square. Blank, it is drawn in ink. Written and
% paid for, it is filled. A statement opens a blank cell in the margin; the
% proof that closes on the page fills it there; a statement with no proof on
% the page keeps its cell open. The cover introduces a restricted view;
% the closing square belongs to the statement ledger. For black-only print, define
% \FlagColour as black before loading this file.
\definecolor{flagred}{RGB}{196,38,26}
\providecommand{\FlagColour}{flagred}
\colorlet{flag}{\FlagColour}

